  <result type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Coordination arrangements for mangrove management are supported (POKJA Mangrove)</narrative>
   </title>
   <reference code="275745" vocabulary="99"></reference>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator: Multi-sectoral mangrove coordination bodies operational at national and subnational level (Number)

Description: This indicator measures the operationalization and functioning of coordination bodies (e.g., National Mangrove Working Group and Provincial-level Mangrove Rehabilitation Teams) that will foster inter-sectoral coordination in mangrove management at the central and sub-national levels. A body will be considered operational if it fulfills these four criteria: 
- Has clear ToR / internal document outlining its functions and governance mechanism 
- Meets at least two times a year, with agenda and dissemination of minutes, meeting the minimum quorum. 
- Prepares an annual report on the state of mangroves in Indonesia/the province.
- Government decree officially establishing the body adopted.</narrative>
    </title>
