  <result type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Facilitating payments for blue carbon (sub-component 1.4)</narrative>
   </title>
   <reference code="275744" vocabulary="99"></reference>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator: Readiness requirements for a blue carbon program are met according to internationally recognized standards.

Description: This indicator measures the development of a blue carbon program eligible for payments in national and international markets, designed according to internationally-recognized standards. A blue carbon program that meets readiness requirements would demonstrate the government&#x2019;s capacity to manage and leverage the benefits from the mangrove ecosystem.  There are four readiness criteria that will be assessed: (1) existence of a reference emissions level (REL) for the program area, (2) existence of a framework to monitor and report on mangrove cover change, (3) existence of a benefit sharing mechanism for a blue carbon program, (4) preparation of a program design document in accordance with an internationally recognized standard (e.g., Verra).  Target is cumulative.</narrative>
    </title>
